{
  "bio": [
    "Cliff Asness is the cofounder, managing partner and chief investment officer of AQR Capital Management, a money management firm with $187 billion in assets under management.",
    "AQR stands for Applied Quantitative Research. It invests based on quantitative and proprietary signals, offering products including hedge funds, mutual funds and separately managed accounts.",
    "The firm is headquartered in Greenwich, Connecticut, with other locations in Bangaluru, Dubai, Hong Kong, London, Munich and Sydney.",
    "A finance Ph.D, Asness is an active researcher and worked in quantitative research for Goldman Sachs before starting AQR in 1998."
  ],
  "about": [
    "Asness backed lawmakers who supported New York's marriage equality initiative and is a board member of the International Rescue Committee.",
    "Asness was a teaching assistant at the University of Chicago for Nobel laureate Eugene Fama, whose efficient market hypothesis popularized passive investing."
  ]
